{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/203651-show-me-your-hunter-characters","id":203651,"title":"Show me your Hunter characters!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-21T02:17:03-07:00","id":203651,"title":"Show me your Hunter characters!","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I'll start with two I'm rather proud of.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Ridley Duquette</b>, ghoul in the service of the Cheiron Group\u2019s FPD. Duquette was the reluctant blood slave of a vampire, but was too thoroughly addicted to the monster\u2019s blood to dream of escaping. When an FPD team kicked in the door and staked his master, Ridley demanded to join up with them; now, he\u2019s one of their top agents. Cheiron keeps the ghoul on a short leash - they supply him with the monthly dose of vampire blood that keeps him alive, and will cut it off if he gets uppity - and treats him like a glorified attack dog. Most agents find him incredibly creepy.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Sidney</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">, a Les Mysteres (Path of the Soul) forced into the tradition by his crazed father. The man was (depending on the day) either a New Age spiritualist who did a lot of LSD in the 60s or the subject of top secret CIA experiments; either way, he isolated and indoctrinated his son. Sidney has escaped and adjusted surprisingly well, but can\u2019t shake the \u2018gifts\u2019 that resulted from his abuse. With no other road ahead of him, he reluctantly takes to the life of a wandering spiritual troubleshooter, all while looking for some peace. </span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I've been trying to come up with a Loyalist of Thule that I like, but I keep getting distracted by Delta Green.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T07:39:12-07:00","id":203837,"title":"","content":"<b>James Sutton [Ex Bear Lodge]: </b>James was (by the end of the chronicle) a twenty two year old man whom grew up in a town that was under the open protection of a pack of Forsaken. The Forsaken treated their Kinfolk well enough, and even taught them a little bit about their heritage and what they could potentially become, if they where blessed enough - but James didn't want that. He wanted a normal life - a wife, children, a job. I mean sure it <i>sounds </i>cool in principle, and that they where chosen for this and whatever, but what if you didn't want it?. What made it worse was that he had to watch his closest childhood friend, Amy, go through her First Change - at which point she stopped being the girl she had been before. She became increasingly violent and distant as the pack adopted her and taught her their ways. A few weeks later, she ended up dead in an encounter with a powerful spirit.<br /> <br /> Now, this <i>could </i>have been the end of it - while bad, it certainly doesn't push one into the life of a hunter, does it? Except James is unknowingly being Urged by a Spirit. Taking a leaf from Hunter: The Reckoning, what James sees an Uratha as - even for a few moments at a glance - is something inhuman and wrong. Something angry. Something that wants to kill everything around it. Which, well, isn't exactly wrong - but that was what he had to suffer through seeing his closest friend become. And so, really, that was that. So he decided he'd hunt down and kill any Uratha he could to protect people from these angry, inhuman super predators. James was only seventeen when he fled the town - but he was a smart kid. He took to the internet and managed to get in contact with The Bear Lodge. James knows quite a lot more than most about the Uratha - which helps him hunt them down. He also acknowledged that if <i>he </i>ever changed, he'd shoot himself in the head with a silver bullet. He'd rather die than become that.<br /> <br /> Over the course of the chronicle I played him in, James proved himself good at tracking and killing Uratha - as is expected of The Bear Lodge. Unfortunately over that same period of time he met a few Wolfblooded whom laid down their lives to protect the Uratha he hunted - some he'd had to kill himself. Maybe it was this or maybe it was the constant Urging of his 'inner voice' (actually the Spirit) but it eventually hit him that <i>every </i>Kinfolk could become an Uratha. An inhuman monster. And slowly, but surely, the Spirit began to poison his view of others like him as well. He'd seen a flash of the Beast that lurked in their blood. A glint of the wolf in their eyes.<br /> <br /> So then he began to hunt Kinfolk and Uratha alike. By the time he was twenty years old, he'd become a Slasher (I believe a brute? An unusual one; he used guns rather than melee weapons) - still hunting Uratha, but also hunting down and slaying Kinfolk to save them from what they could become and the danger they could cause others. The Cell he'd been hunting with eventually had to hunt him down, but they didn't manage to kill him.<br /> <br /> James was - <i>is </i>- definitely my favourite Hunter I've ever had the pleasure of playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/128x125q90/90/w20supportergarou125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1612-mabs","user":"Mabs","date":". 07-21-2014, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1612-mabs","name":"Mabs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T17:17:19-07:00","id":204397,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Brian Grossman</b></span> - <b>The Union</b>: Ex-vampire slave-turned enforcer for The Union in Tampa Bay. Was killing plenty of vampires in Tampa Bay until he ran into a bit of trouble in Miami involving the God-Machine. Ended up stabbing two cops to death, knocked out a Mage with a punch and lost the lower half of his arm from a grenade. Things got a bit too crazy for him near the end, and had to back out and go back to doing what he did best: hunt vampires. With one arm.<br /> <br /> I love this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T22:18:52-07:00","id":205707,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:GF Ordner Inverted\"><b><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">I never actually played this character, except maybe for a half a session. It was mostly a joke, and another player was Dani.</span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:GF Ordner Inverted\"><b>Wayward Son: Sean Colt</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>The teacher and his sister now travel around the country hunting down the things that go bump in the night, and draining leeches of their blood to feed Danielle's addiction and keep her from suffering the crippling nature of Vitae withdrawal. They've gained a bit of a reputation among other hunters, but they always try to keep their natures secret. Sean keeps his leg covered, so that no one sees the burned, black lines that form a sealing sigil. Danielle tries to keep from using her unnatural speed, strength, or healing.</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GF Ordner Inverted\"><b><i>Character Sheet</i></b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>Intelligence\u25cf\u25cf, Wits \u25cf\u25cf, Resolve \u25cf\u25cf<br /> Strength \u25cf\u25cf, Dexterity \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Stamina \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Presence \u25cf, Manipulation \u25cf\u25cf, Composure \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>Investigation \u25cf\u25cf, Medicine \u25cf, Occult \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> Athletics \u25cf\u25cf, Brawl \u25cf\u25cf, Drive \u25cf, Firearms \u25cf\u25cf, Weaponry \u25cf<br /> Persuasion \u25cf, Streetwise \u25cf, Subterfuge \u25cf\u25cf</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GF Ordner Inverted\"><b><i>Specialties</i></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>Medicine - Patch-up</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>&quot;It's just like sewing a button back on... 'Cept it hurts like a motherfucker.&quot;</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>Occult - Identifying magic </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>&quot;I know what that spell is, and I'm not gonna let you get it off.&quot;</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>Larceny - Forgery</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>&quot; Looks real, huh?&quot;</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>Subterfuge - Impersonating authority </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>&quot;We're here with the health department.&quot;</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GF Ordner Inverted\"><b><i>Merits</i></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>Gifted: Copper (\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b> - By concentrating his will and waving a hand, Sean can cause air to solidify in front of him as a spongiform barrier with Durability equal to the Successes. Resolve+Science+Gifted, 6 Dice.</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>Gifted: Telekinesis (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b> - With an expenditure of Willpower, the former teacher can extend his mind to lift objects up to Size 4. While Sean's mind isn't what it used to be, he can still use this power to attack, with the roll subtracting Defense and Armour from the target. Intelligence+Occult+Gifted, 8 dice.</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>Fame (\u2022)</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b> - Sean and his sister are well known among those who hunt monsters. When dealing with other Hunters who might know of his reputation, he gains +1 to Social rolls. The rumours say that he's driven, and would do anything for his sister, and to destroy monsters, especially those bloodsucking leeches. Others say that he's as monstrous as the things he puts in the ground.</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>Safehouse - Denise:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b> Durability: 3 Size: 12 Structure: 15 Acceleration: 26(35 mph/turn) Safe Speed: 110(75 mph) Maximum Speed: 220(150 mph) Handling: 3 Occupancy: 1+3</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>-- Size (X</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>) - The old red Chevrolet Camaro isn't the greatest safehouse, but it is portable.</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>-- Cache (</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>)</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b> - The trunk pops open, and hidden beneath it is a compartment for storing all kinds of things that need to be hidden.</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>Multilingual (\u2022)</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b> - The teacher has lost a lot, but he's also learned. He can't speak it well, but he knows both Aramaic and Enochian well enough to chant a demon back to Hell, or recite an incantation. If he needs to say something quick, he needs to roll Wits+Academics, or to read it he needs to roll Int+Academics.</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>Talisman (\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>\u2022\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>)</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b> - Evans' Jacket. Blood sigils line the inside of the jacket, tracing out, roughly, the human circulatory system. There's a torn Canadian flag on the shoulder, and over the heart is a white symbol of protection stitched fresh and white. The jacket provides 1/0 protection until the symbol is touched with an effort of will. This sends out a serious of previously undetectable, pale blue lines, forming into intricate patterns of Enochian protection symbols. The centerpiece of the jacket is a representation of Robert Flood's Sephirothic Tree of Life.</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GF Ordner Inverted\"><b><i>Flaws</i></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b>Bad Leg -Sean's base speed is -2, and it hurts to push himself when walking. He has to stop every once in a while and give his leg a rest.<br /> Tell (Calling Card)- Whenever he's on a Hunt, he has a habit of writing out the phrase &quot;<i>Wer mit Ungeheuern k\u00e4mpft, mag zusehn, dass er nicht dabei zum Ungeheuer wird. Und wenn du lange in einen Abgrund blickst, blickt der Abgrund auch in dich hinein</i>.&quot; No, the passage may not refer to literal monsters, but it\u2019s a common enough quote that it still keeps coming to mind. Once or twice, he's even caught himself carving it into a window sill while watching someone.<br /> Secrets -</b></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b><b> A multitude.</b></b></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b><i>The first that he sold his soul, and barely clawed it back.</i></b></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b><i>The second that his sister is a ghoul.</i></b></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b><i>The third that he dabbles with the same powers that make sorcerers and witches.</i></b></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Gentium\"><b><i>The fourth, and possibly most damning, that he slew another Hunter, and took his jacket and journal.</i></b></span></span></span></li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T23:50:00-07:00","id":205781,"title":"","content":"My favorite hunter, who got killed by his own cell, was a man named Eli, and his friend, the Strix.<br /> <br /> Eli came from a long line of hunters that stopped with his mother. She refused to indulge in the family lunacy and instead settled down outside of Boston. She got married had three kids, Anna who got into the antique business, Eli who joined the Marines and lost a leg, and Drake who only recently moved out and is the lead vocalist for a death metal band. The whole family got together one Sunday for dinner and when they got home, Edgar, their grandfather, was laying on the couch, bleeding slightly and looking haggard. He refused to go to the hospital, instead he had Eli help patch him up, asked Anna for the some information about something, and slept on the couch. The wound looked suspiciously like teeth marks, but Eli never got the chance to ask, because Edgar was gone in the morning. Anna, Eli and Drake decided to try and find the grandfather they never knew.<br /> <br /> They found him on Tuesday night, slipping into a Southie Warehouse. Leaving all sense behind them, they followed after their elder. What they saw in the building was obscene; cannibalism, blood, occult symbols and lots of shadowy owls in the rafters. They became even more worried for the old man and hurried along faster. As he had the most experience, Eli lead the group, his pistol out. They arrived just in time to see their grandfather hew through someone's skull with an axe. A tablet stood on an altar, surrounded by fire, blood and empty-eyed people with gore stained hands. The People were attacking Edgar, and without pause, Eli began firing into the group of 8 people.<br /> <br /> The firefight was intense, but Anna couldn't take her eyes off of the tablet, and picked her way over to it. Eli's gun clicked empty, just as his sister grasped the tablet, and Edgar shouted <i>something</i>. Without thinking, without hesitation, Marine and Brother clicked into place, and Eli sprinted to his sister, the prosthetic ripping into his leg. He slipped on the gore, the leg snapped and he fell head long into his sister, dislodging her grip and spattering his blood across the tablet moments before it shattered on the concrete. The Spirit in the tablet, the same beast who drove these humans into a frenzy of blood, was the Strix. With its vessels dead, Strix had only one place to go, other than pieces. It used the blood sympathy with Eli and climbed into his body.<br /> <br /> What followed was a wholly spiritual battle that ended in a stalemate. Strix was too well fed to be dislodged, and Eli was too willful to be overcome; the two were stuck together, constantly fighting for dominance. Each personality bled into the other, Eli slowly became more and more merciless and vengeful even without Strix taking control. In game he: firebombed an apartment complex because it also had vampires; shot a werewolf in the head with a .45 at pointblank range (and said &quot;Bad Doggie!) because it was putting the moves on his sister; shot a cell mate in the head while eating at Denny's because the cell mate wanted to &quot;borrow&quot; someone else's soul, permanently. About five seconds after killing the other cell mate, he got hit with an epically successful cryokenesis attack from another cell mate, and died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T10:07:04-07:00","id":231624,"title":"","content":"Eric Mattick-Former detective for the Seattle PD. <br /> Mattick had just been declared the youngest detective to make homicide. Bright, determined, good instincts. Double major in criminal justice, and biology. He was a CSI character almost made flesh. Outside the job, Mattick was a conspiracy theorist who whole heartedly believed in alien abduction and ancient astronaut theories. If not woeking on cases, he was either researching alien sightings or blogging about aliens. His partner, senior detective -Seargent O'houlihan thought he was a niave kid with a brifht future if he would just shut up. Then the weird cases came...and Mattick ate it up. The due were deemed the &quot;mulder/scully&quot; duo and ridiculed over cases involving suspects with glowing eyes, suspects who ate all the neighborhood pets, or practiced strange rituals. After getting a case that involved a high ranking employee of a major pharmecutical corp, Mattick fell into the deep end of supernaturals pulling strings in politics and business. He was framed for murder, terrorism, and corruption. It was then that he left Seattle and teamed up wirh several other victims of this pharma company.<br /> Mattick now travels with his fellow &quot;burned and blacklisted&quot; cellmates trying to gather evidence to clear their names while trying to find a way to hit back at the supernatural baddies who forced them into the vigil. He still blogs about aliens, even though he has yet to see one among the scores of shapechangers, vampires, ghosts, possesed dolls, and the case that dealt with pod people...turns out it was a fungi like thing living in the local water resevoir that had a hive mind link. His blog is linked to Network zero, though he has no actual status with them. He has recently picked up a mentor while in Boston, a catholic preist who helped exercise a demon from an innocent girl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T10:37:39-07:00","id":238319,"title":"","content":"Sorry for derailing this thread a little, but I have a question. Do you use Hunter for combat focused games or more investigative? I see a lot of characters in this topic, who killed a lot. So that's why. My games are a lot like the previous post from ManBearPig btw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1873,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","user":"Jan Paparazzi","date":". 08-23-2014, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T11:20:01-07:00","id":238368,"title":"","content":"The hunter game I play Mattick in is an &quot;On the road&quot; game now, with about a 70/30 combat to investigation focus currently. The hunter game im running is going to be like ours started, with that ratio flipped. The group for my game made a homicide seargent, a forensic analyst, an information broker, and a drug dealer's muscle. Since I plan to introduce the supernatural very slowly, its planned to be investigation focused for a good while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T11:58:06-07:00","id":238408,"title":"","content":"Eli was the way he was because the group I was in was so totally focused on plotting, planning, discussing and debating. We'd go whole through a month worth of sessions and not get anywhere meaningful, so I wrote an action hero to liven things up.<br /> <br /> To contrast to Eli, my second favorite hunter was Arthur Bishop. Arthur was a horror writer, whose writing caught the eye of a Vampire. Within a month she turned his life around, dragged everything he wrote to super-stardom, and had him completely reliant on her. He only escaped because the vampire's fickle attention turned elsewhere, leaving him in the gutter without a dime. He kept writing, but without her influence, Arthur could get nowhere and came up with a crazy idea: the best way to write horror and monsters is to see them first hand! He ended up dying before hitting it big again, but he was the biggest proponent of researching and investigating I've ever played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2861,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","user":"Nyx","date":". 08-23-2014, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T01:38:47-07:00","id":242093,"title":"","content":"I've got a Hunter idea that's been in the wings ever since Mortal Remains came out. Haven't had the chance to use it yet but I'm very proud of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Edgar L. Noran</b>, author of a popular series of fantasy novels and one of the Faithful of Shulpae. Edgar grew up caught between two worlds. His mother was an honest, god fearing christian who taught her son the importance of virtue and standing up for what's right. His father on the other hand was one of the Faithful of Shulpae who taught his son that the Gods were amoral beings and that the only way to give them true worship and respect was through the amoral act of the Feast. Having to keep his father's lessons a secret was tough enough on a child, but nothing could have prepared him for his rite of passage and first Feast. The nightmares he endured and the sickness that followed as his body reacted to the &quot;God's Blessings&quot; nearly drove him over the edge. Thankfully both of his parents encouraged his love of writing stories from a young age, and it was through examining his condition through stories that let him get past those difficult times. It's also what made him a household name in the current day.<br /> <br /> Now thirty-two years old and having started publishing his second series of novels Edgar balances his career as an writer with his duties as a Guide for the local Temple of the Faithful. He uses his novels to subtly warn the public about the dangers of the World of Darkness whilst simultaneously scouting for potential additions to the Faithful's ranks. Unfortunately he's had very little success in this regard thanks to the current market being flooded with fantasy novels. However, his connections to the art community and network of fans has proven invaluable when it comes to scouting for hidden Gods to hunt for the Feast. He rarely takes part in the actual hunt, preferring to leave the capture of the God to more skilled warriors, yet continually surprises his fellow hunters with his skill at coordinating ambushes and traps.<br /> <br /> Edgar has come to an amicable peace with his faith and morals, seeing that the Faithful's hunt for the divine has brought more good to humanity than harm, but deep down he knows that the Faithful walk a very fine line between apotheosis and damnation. One that gets harder to see as time rolls on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Grammar 08-28-2014, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T18:46:53-07:00","id":242762,"title":"","content":"<b>Sir Larcen Cruise, The Fortune Hunter</b><br /> Apparently a very fit young British gentleman, Larcen is famed as a writer of 'Historical Fantasy', particularly the &quot;Fortune Hunter's Guide&quot; series which details actual supernatural events and goings-on in the world, spanning back for over a century. Larcen himself was born in 1873, and first encountered the supernatural at the age of 17, when he visited a newly-unearthed pyramid and met its owner face-to-face. After surviving that encounter and putting the mummy 'back to sleep' long enough to get away, he travelled to America and learned from Old West outlaws how to ride and shoot and survive in the wild.<br /> That is also when he started to write his books, starting of course with &quot;The Fortune Hunter's Guide to Egypt&quot;. At the turn of the century, Larcen and his cell of American 'Gentlemen of Violence' prevented an extradimensional entity from engulfing New York City. During that ordeal, Larcen was exposed to some unearthly energies that seem to have been what has endowed him with unnaturally long life. Indeed, he has not aged a day since.<br /> In modern times, he is fabulously wealthy and his moniker 'The Fortune Hunter' is known through the supernatural world, a sort of bogeyman for the bogeymen. He spends most of his time looking for magical artifacts from long ago or hunting the very rarest and deadliest of monsters. To stave off boredom in-between these pursuits, each generation he takes on one protege or a handful of students at the most, and teaches them what he knows. And he knows a lot.<br /> <br /> This was a favorite character of mine for a game set in the 1890's, that ended up a powerful Mentor for PC's in a modern-era game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/550-redline","name":"Redline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}